  <!-- § 10 projections: inputs climate-cmip6-windows-temp, climate-cmip6-windows-hotdays, climate-cmip6-windows-heatstress, climate-cmip6-states-temp -->
  <section>
    <div class="sec-head"><span class="no">10</span><h2>A child born today</h2><span class="line"></span><span class="unit">CMIP6 projections, change from 1995-2014; model output, not data</span></div>
    <div class="break">
      <figure id="cb-proj" style="margin:0">
        <div class="plate-head">
          <div class="t">
            <h3>In the years a child born in {born} turns 54 to 73, India is projected to be {fmt.num1(pt("ssp126", 2080).med)} to {fmt.num1(pt("ssp585", 2080).med)}°C warmer than in 1995-2014, depending on emissions</h3>
            <div class="sub">Projected change in India's annual mean temperature from 1995-2014, °C, for four 20-year windows and four emission pathways. Dot: the median of about 30 models; bar: the 10th to 90th percentile across them.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="plate-val"><div class="v acc" id="pv-proj">{sd1(pt("ssp245", 2080).med)}</div><div class="c">SSP2-4.5, 2080-2099, median</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="frame">
          <div class="plotzone" id="plot-proj" set:html={CH.proj(C)} />
          <div class="plotfoot">
            <span class="src">Source: CMIP6 multi-model ensemble, downscaled and bias-corrected by the World Bank CCKP. Projections under stated scenarios, not forecasts.</span>
            <span class="dl"><button data-dl="svg">SVG</button><button data-dl="png">PNG</button><button data-dl="csv">CSV</button><a href="https://climateknowledgeportal.worldbank.org/country/india/climate-data-projections" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Source</a></span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="explain">
          <div class="ev">
            <span class="mk">How to read this</span>
            <p>Each group is a 20-year window; within it, one dot per emissions pathway. The pathways barely differ until the 2040s, because the warming of the next two decades is largely set by gases already emitted. After that the choice of pathway decides most of the outcome. A child born in {born} is 14 to 33 years old in the 2040-2059 window and 54 to 73 in 2080-2099.</p>
            <p>The baseline here is 1995-2014, the models' reference period, not 1951-1980. The models' change from 1995-2014 cannot be added to the observed change since 1951 to make one number: they are different instruments.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="now">
            <span class="mk">As of CMIP6, CCKP {P.windows[0]} to 2099</span>
            <p>2040-2059: <b id="ex-p-245-40">{sd1(pt("ssp245", 2040).med)}</b> under SSP2-4.5 (range {sd1(pt("ssp245", 2040).p10)} to {sd1(pt("ssp245", 2040).p90)}), {sd1(pt("ssp585", 2040).med)} under SSP5-8.5. 2080-2099: <b id="ex-p-126-80">{sd1(pt("ssp126", 2080).med)}</b> under SSP1-2.6, {sd1(pt("ssp245", 2080).med)} under SSP2-4.5, {sd1(pt("ssp370", 2080).med)} under SSP3-7.0 and <b id="ex-p-585-80">{sd1(pt("ssp585", 2080).med)}</b> under SSP5-8.5.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </figure>
    </div>

    <div class="break" style="margin-top:104px">
      <figure id="cb-proj-heat" style="margin:0">
        <div class="plate-head">
          <div class="t">
            <h3>Days of extreme humid heat are projected to multiply {fmt.num1(pd("hi41", "ssp245", 2040) / pref("hi41"))} times by mid-century, nights of 26°C or more by {fmt.count(100 * (pd("tr26", "ssp245", 2040) / pref("tr26") - 1))}%</h3>
            <div class="sub">Projected days a year at an average spot in India, for 20-year windows, under SSP2-4.5 (blue) and SSP5-8.5 (red), ensemble median; the grey line is the models' own 1995-2014 level.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="plate-val"><div class="v acc" id="pv-projheat">{days(pd("tr26", "ssp245", 2040))}</div><div class="c">nights of 26°C or more, 2040-2059, SSP2-4.5</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="frame">
          <div class="plotzone" id="plot-proj-heat" set:html={CH.projHeat(C)} />
          <div class="plotfoot">
            <span class="src">Source: CMIP6 multi-model ensemble median, indices by the World Bank CCKP. CCKP's projected wet-bulb series for India are corrupt at source (an India mean near 8°C) and are not used.</span>
            <span class="dl"><button data-dl="svg">SVG</button><button data-dl="png">PNG</button><button data-dl="csv">CSV</button><a href="https://climateknowledgeportal.worldbank.org/country/india/climate-data-projections" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Source</a></span>
